\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Derived a reflection-symmetric local cusp and an explicit symmetry-compatible degeneracy, giving a concrete nondegeneracy test. No actual Kerr caustic or any bundled observational/strong-field comparison is computed.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied complete definition, catalogue wording, scope qualifications and source list for this canonical ID. The original-source citations are inherited as supplied references; no fresh primary-source or novelty search was performed for this attempt. No current open-status claim is inferred from this calculation.

\paragraph{A local cusp test compatible with reflection symmetry.}Let a smooth two-dimensional lens map \(F(s,t)=(X,Y)\) obey \(X(s,-t)=X(s,t)\) and \(Y(s,-t)=-Y(s,t)\), as a chosen equatorial-symmetry chart would. The elementary normal-form example
\[F(s,t)=(s,t^3+st)
\]
has Jacobian determinant \(J=3t^2+s\). Its critical set is \(s=-3t^2\), and the caustic image is \((-3t^2,-2t^3)\), which satisfies \(27Y^2+4X^3=0\). At nonzero \(t\), the critical image has nonzero derivative and is a fold arc; at zero both first derivatives vanish and the cubic cusp is visible explicitly.
\paragraph{A symmetry-only failure.}The map \(F_0(s,t)=(s,st)\) has the same reflection parity but critical set \(s=0\), whose entire image is one point. Thus reflection symmetry and a vanishing Jacobian do not force a stable cusp; a nonzero cubic transverse derivative and a suitable mixed derivative are genuine extra conditions. Nor does this local cusp calculation produce a global astroid or count higher-order sheets.
\paragraph{Remaining Kerr scope.}One must compute these derivatives from an actual Kerr null-geodesic endpoint map in specified observer/source coordinates and establish nondegeneracy in a declared strong-deflection regime. That is the first gap. Off-equatorial and higher-order images, global caustic shapes, effective coordinates, observational accessibility, the historical MAXIM project, gas/MHD modelling, and comparison of time delays and critical curves with shifted Schwarzschild remain outside this local test. No numerical Kerr integration or observational prediction was performed.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked critical set, cusp elimination equation, fold derivative, degenerate symmetric example and all broad lensing/model/observational limitations. This was an LLM adversarial audit, not independent human verification; no theorem prover was used. Prompts A then B applied to this ID: Checked critical set, cusp elimination equation, fold derivative, degenerate symmetric example and all broad lensing/model/observational limitations. Scope remains limited: Evaluate and control the relevant Jacobian jets for the actual Kerr endpoint map in specified coordinates and strong-deflection scaling.

Coordinator checked the cusp determinant, critical image equation and symmetry-preserving degenerate comparison map. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

